# GYST Microservices Project

## Context Files - READ THESE FIRST
When starting any task, reference:
- .context/00-PROJECT-OVERVIEW.md (always read first)
- .context/01-ARCHITECTURE/dual-mode-deployment.md (for architecture questions)
- .context/03-MICROSERVICES/service-template-guide.md (when building services)
- .context/05-DATABASE/supabase-schema.sql (for database questions)
- .context/07-EXAMPLES/dual-mode-service-complete.py (for code examples)
- .context/10-WIRASM-CONTEXT/prp-methodology.md (for understanding PRPs)

## Code Standards
- Python 3.11+ with type hints everywhere
- Use Pydantic for all data models
- Follow dual-mode deployment pattern (internal + external)
- Always include customer_id for data isolation
- Use structured JSON logging
- Include /health and /metrics endpoints on all services

## Testing Requirements
- Write tests before marking task complete
- Test both internal and external modes separately
- Use pytest
- Validate multi-tenant isolation

## When Building Services
1. Follow service template from .context/03-MICROSERVICES/service-template-guide.md
2. Support both deployment modes (internal + external)
3. Use config files (config/internal.yaml and config/external.yaml)
4. Always isolate data by customer_id
5. Include health and metrics endpoints

## Database
- All tables with customer data MUST have customer_id column
- Always filter queries by customer_id
- Use Supabase (schema in .context/05-DATABASE/supabase-schema.sql)

## Critical Rules
- NEVER hardcode API keys or secrets
- ALWAYS use environment variables
- NEVER skip customer_id in database queries
- ALWAYS log with correlation IDs
